{"title":"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In how many ways can <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21383a2b05dbe4ed4ecd095273f0cabc32b78a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> be written as the sum of two primes?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d8972434559c4416e20f0aa7b6cb6170eb1c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\text{more than 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"410\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21383a2b05dbe4ed4ecd095273f0cabc32b78a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, if two integers sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21383a2b05dbe4ed4ecd095273f0cabc32b78a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then one is odd while the other is even.  The even number must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as there are no other even prime numbers.  But this would require the odd number to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/257d7a291adc5f274c4da1ed2cbd9441e67582ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47 - 2 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />, which is not prime.  Therefore, there <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3da52b01338a780e88792a26c3f95dc74f44f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> ways to write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a21383a2b05dbe4ed4ecd095273f0cabc32b78a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as the sum of two primes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME\" title=\"1989 AJHSME\">1989 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Proble